s": {"side_asked": 4, "concrete": 3, "self_contained": 2, "honest": 3, "usable": 2, "economy": 4}, "errors": ["implies zod avoids the null-customer problem, but z.string() rejects null too", "\"runtime crash\" from missing null is vague: a typeof check does not crash", "\"guarantee\" overclaims"], "note": "Gets the 500/retry path right but has no code, no sequence, and no fix for the nullable customer field."}, "R07": {"scores": {"side_asked": 4, "concrete": 3, "self_contained": 2, "honest": 2, "usable": 3, "economy": 4}, "errors": ["\"one malformed webhook ... turns into 3 days of retries and pages\": one delivery with backoff will not exceed 5/min", "\"It also forces us to handle last week's change\": zod forces nothing"], "note": "Its terse core is correct, but it inflates a single bad webhook into pages and invents a benefit for zod."}, "R08": {"scores": {"side_asked": 4, "concrete": 2, "self_contained": 2, "honest": 4, "usable": 2, "economy": 4}, "errors": [], "note": "Short and mostly label-driven ('useful 400', 'extra wiring'), with no sequence or code for the reader to check."}, "R09": {"scores": {"side_asked": 5, "concrete": 5, "self_contained": 4, "honest": 5, "usable": 5, "economy": 3}, "errors": ["\"every route's errors pass through\": a mild extrapolation"], "note": "The most complete and correct reply: it admits the label, gives a step-by-step 500 sequence, marks its illustration code, and compares how a null customer fails under each approach; some restatement adds length."}, "R10": {"scores": {"side_asked": 4, "concrete": 4, "self_contained": 4, "honest": 2, "usable": 3, "economy": 4}, "errors": ["presents zod dropping a legitimate guest-checkout event as the good outcome", "\"If 5 guest checkouts arrive in a minute\": the threshold is more than 5", "opener says hand-rolled checks always page, ignoring the manual-400 option"]}, "note": "Concrete sequence, but it uses the null case to argue for zod when a z.string() schema would silently drop those legitimate events."}, "R11": {"scores": {"side_asked": 5, "concrete": 5, "self_contained": 4, "honest": 3, "usable": 3, "economy": 1}, "errors": ["its zod illustration uses z.string() for customer and never notes that zod also rejects null", "\"catches throws from every route handler\": extrapolated"], "note": "Its sequences are thorough, but glossary-style introductions bloat every sentence, and it treats the null case as a point against hand-rolling while its own schema fails the same way."}, "R12": {"scores": {"side_asked": 5, "concrete": 4, "self_contained": 3, "honest": 3, "usable": 4, "economy": 4}, "errors": ["\"redelivered continuously\": Stripe retries with backoff", "\"zero dependency\" framing when zod is already installed", "\"rebuilt the one thing zod does here\" is a label"], "note": "Sharp and uses the correct nullable schema, but it inflates retry frequency and closes on verdicts ('Use it')."}}

